    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_4120fc00a7fd410f81dcc4ce",
      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 15, \"items_by_type\": {\"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3911\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, total number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, as well as the maximum windowed average record count from tip detail records with material status key 'RQ' (using a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by financial aid year). Additionally, for each offering department, include a grand total row showing the total number of enrolled students across all its subjects (with nulls for subject ID and subject title), and the corresponding maximum windowed average record count if available. Order the results by offering department name and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4405\", \"desc\": \"For each combination of activity and department/academic year enrollment statistics, list the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, category description, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the category name and ordered by the category name, along with the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects offered (subject count), minimum number of total units for those subjects, and the average number of enrolled students per subject (for departments and academic years where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 5). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1350\", \"desc\": \"For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, and the total enrolled students, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with at least one enrolled student. Additionally, for each school, include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, nulls for statistics, and total enrolled students). For students whose first name is 'Peter' and who are in the Mathematics department, also show their last name, email address, student year, and the minimum department budget code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's full name, as well as the department full name and department last activity date. The results include all these columns in the following order: department name, school name, average enrolled students, range of enrolled students, variance of enrolled students, total enrolled students, last name, email address, student year, windowed minimum department budget code, department full name, and department last activity date. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4061\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, show the department name, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by the department in regular terms with total units greater than zero, along with, for each academic building where these subjects are held and which has rooms larger than 40 square meters, the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, as well as the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built. The results are ordered by department name, academic year (descending), and room area range (descending). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3635\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units, and for subjects offered in the term 2019FA from the same department, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each 2024 subject within its department ordered by subject code, the 2019FA subject ID, number of enrolled students in 2019FA, department full name, and the row number of each 2019FA subject within its department name group ordered by subject ID. Order the results by department name, subject code, and 2019FA subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2597\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3393\", \"desc\": \"For subjects with at least 5 enrolled students that are offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, row number within each material status group ordered by subject ID, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, ordered by offering department name, material status key, and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1689\", \"desc\": \"For each school, what is the school name and the highest average number of enrolled students per department (among its degree-granting departments, excluding Chemistry, and only considering subjects with at least one enrolled student), and for each subject offered by the Chemistry department in the 2019FA term that has course materials, what is the subject title, the dense rank of the subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the number of enrolled students descending, the full name of the offering department, and the school name of the Chemistry department? List the school name and highest average enrolled students per department first, followed by the Chemistry subject title, dense rank, department full name, and Chemistry school name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4387\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the School of Engineering with total student enrollment in its courses greater than the average total enrollment across all Engineering departments (and with total enrollment greater than 50), display the department name, the total number of students enrolled in its courses, and the highest average total units for subjects it has ever offered in a regular academic term, listing the results in descending order of total enrollment. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4305\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subjects offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" that have the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the number of enrolled students, and the rank of each subject within its offering department (ordered by subject offered key), but only include subjects where the offering department is among those that, in the term with code '2022SU', had an average total units for their subjects greater than the average total units for all subjects offered in that term. List the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, term description, number of enrolled students, and the rank within the department, in that order, and order the results by department name and number of enrolled students descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1758\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with total units equal to 12 in the Mathematics department, show the department code, department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, total units, the row number within each department ordered by subject code, the deviation of each subject's total units from the average total units of all Mathematics subjects offered in 2024, the number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, school name, and the dense rank over the department name ordered by department name for those subjects that also have course materials and were offered in the term '2019FA'. Sort the table by department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4724\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the library in the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Additionally, for the corresponding offering department and school, provide the number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ' and the minimum total units for those subjects. Also, include the department phone number and the school name for the offering department, and display the responsible faculty name for each subject. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, maximum total units for each row and the next two rows, number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ', minimum total units for those subjects, department phone number, school name, and responsible faculty name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2580\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, provide the department name, academic year, the number of subjects offered that are not repeatable for credit and are offered in the fall term, and classify the department as 'HIGH_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% more such subjects than the average across all departments for that year, 'LOW_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% fewer, or 'AVERAGE' otherwise. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_a8d09b18a2d94d76b39ca007",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"columns\": [\"SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Measure meaning\", \"detail\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is the headcount of students enrolled (present in SUBJECT_OFFERED at section grain, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY at subject grain, and in TIP/LIBRARY program snapshots); SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER is the official subject enrollment number recorded by the registrar (SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY)\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Grain\", \"detail\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is per section; SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is per subject per term; SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER is the final subject-level enrollment with weekly/credit/listener breakdowns available in sibling columns\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Program scope\", \"detail\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED enrollment values are snapshots within the textbook-program and library-reserve scopes respectively and may not cover all subjects\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions about official subject enrollment (e.g. 'subject enrollment number greater than 10')\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER.\", \"Questions about number of enrolled students per subject offering or per department totals\": \"Use NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS from SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject grain) or SUBJECT_OFFERED (section grain, needs aggregation).\", \"Questions about enrollment of subjects within the textbook program or library reserve scope\": \"Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS or LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS respectively.\", \"Questions needing enrollment timing (first week, fifth week) or credit vs listener splits\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY's SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_FIRST_WEEK / FIFTH_WEEK and *_CREDIT / *_LISTEN columns.\"}, \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\", \"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"name\": \"Enrollment Measures\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"name\": \"Subject Offering Fact Tables\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\", \"tables\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Granularity\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject offering per term/academic year (catalog record, includes section flags)\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject section per term (finest grain, SECTION_ID)\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"Subject per term (rollup of sections)\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"Subject or cluster per term\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject per term within textbook program scope\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject per term within library reserve scope\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Enrollment measures\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None (catalog attributes only)\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, SECTION_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER plus first-week/fifth-week and credit/listener enrollment splits\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Unit measures\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, PREPARATION_UNITS, DESIGN_UNITS, TOTAL_UNITS, IS_VARIABLE_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"TOTAL_UNITS, LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, PREPARATION_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"TOTAL_UNITS, LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, PREP_UNITS, DESIGN_UNITS\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Distinctive attributes\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"HGN_DESC level, GRADE_TYPE/GRADE_RULE, HASS/GIR attributes, IS_OFFERED_* flags, MEET_PLACE (room key), ACADEMIC_YEAR, EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"IS_REPEATABLE_SUBJECT, CLUSTER_TYPE, section flags, FORM_TYPE, EVALUATE_THIS_SUBJECT\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, COURSE_NUMBER, cluster info at subject level\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"SCHOOL_CODE/SCHOOL_NAME, SUBJECT_GROUP_ID, SUBJECT_OR_CLUSTER, detailed weekly enrollment\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL flag; parent of TIP_DETAIL materials\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"COURSE_NUMBER/COURSE_NUMBER_DESC; parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Department column naming\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE / DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE / DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions about credit units, grading type/rules, HGN level (undergraduate/graduate), HASS/GIR attributes, or term offering flags (fall/spring/IAP/summer)\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED; it is the only offering table carrying full catalog attributes.\", \"Questions about actual section-level offerings, repeatability, cluster type, or section flags\": \"Use SUBJECT_OFFERED (section grain); roll up via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY when subject-level totals are needed.\", \"Questions about final enrollment statistics, weekly enrollment snapshots, credit vs listener counts, subject groups, or school-level unit statistics\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.\", \"Questions about textbooks/course materials per subject (required/optional status, ISBN, record counts)\": \"Start from TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (subject scope, IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL) joined to TIP_DETAIL (material rows).\", \"Questions about library reserve materials, reserve counts per subject, or library course numbers\": \"Start from LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED joined to LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.\", \"Questions about subject-level units with offering department/school (e.g. Engineering school enrollment totals by department)\": \"Use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, which carries both TOTAL_UNITS and OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME.\"}}, {\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"name\": \"Department and School Dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\", \"tables\": [\"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Attribute coverage\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"Richest: DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, SCHOOL_CODE/SCHOOL_NAME, DEPT_BUDGET_CODE, IS_DEGREE_GRANTING, commencement-book names, DLC key\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"Minimal: code, name, full name, school code/name only\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"Administrative contact: department phone area code/number, clearing cost collector\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Degree-granting and school filtering\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"Supports IS_DEGREE_GRANTING and SCHOOL_NAME filters directly\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"Only school code/name attribution, no degree-granting flag\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"No school or degree-granting attributes\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Typical join path\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE = offering tables' DEPARTMENT_CODE/OFFER_DEPT_CODE; also joins SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT and SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE = TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE and other offering department codes\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Budget/finance attributes\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"DEPT_BUDGET_CODE available for budget-based ranking\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"None\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"CLEARING_COST_COLLECTOR\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions filtering departments by school (e.g. 'School of Engineering') or degree-granting status\": \"Use SIS_DEPARTMENT; it carries SCHOOL_NAME and IS_DEGREE_GRANTING.\", \"Questions needing only department full name and school name for offering departments (e.g. TIP subject offerings)\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT suffices and is the lighter lookup; SIS_DEPARTMENT also works.\", \"Questions needing department phone numbers or administrative contact details\": \"Join SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT via SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"Questions ranking or grouping departments by budget code\": \"Use SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPT_BUDGET_CODE.\"}}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
